{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "L{sin(x)}(s) = 1/(s^2 + 1)\n  region of convergence: Re(s) > 0\n  one-sided: f(x) for x >= 0 (0 before)\n  rules: sin/cos table\n  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = 1/2, 3/2, 4: max relative difference 1.8e-16\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "laplace", "ucas": "laplace sin(x)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "laplace", "region_of_convergence": "Re(s) > 0", "roc": "Re(s) > 0", "one_sided": "f(x) for x >= 0 (0 before)", "rules": "sin/cos table", "lhs": "L{sin(x)}(s)", "value": "1/(s^2 + 1)", "headline": "L{sin(x)}(s) = 1/(s^2 + 1)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = 1/2, 3/2, 4: max relative difference 1.8e-16"}], "files": [], "text": "L{sin(x)}(s) = 1/(s^2 + 1)\n  region of convergence: Re(s) > 0\n  one-sided: f(x) for x >= 0 (0 before)\n  rules: sin/cos table\n  check: matches int_0^inf f(t) e^(-st) dt (Gauss-Kronrod) at s = 1/2, 3/2, 4: max relative difference 1.8e-16\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "L^-1{1/(s^2 + 1)}(t) = sin(t)\n  poles: s = +-i\n  for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > 0 (right of every pole)\n  check: transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 1.8e-16\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "ilaplace", "ucas": "ilaplace 1/(s^2+1)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ilaplace", "poles": "s = +-i", "roc": "Re(s) > 0", "lhs": "L^-1{1/(s^2 + 1)}(t)", "value": "sin(t)", "headline": "L^-1{1/(s^2 + 1)}(t) = sin(t)", "details": ["for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > 0 (right of every pole)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 1.8e-16"}], "files": [], "text": "L^-1{1/(s^2 + 1)}(t) = sin(t)\n  poles: s = +-i\n  for t >= 0 (0 before): the right-sided inverse, region of convergence Re(s) > 0 (right of every pole)\n  check: transformed back (Gauss-Kronrod), it matches F at s = 1, 2, 7/2: max relative difference 1.8e-16\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Z{n}(z) = z/(z - 1)^2\n  in powers of z^-1: z^-1/(1 - 2z^-1 + z^-2)\n  region of convergence: |z| > 1\n  one-sided: x[n] for n >= 0\n  rules: n x[n] -> -z X'(z)\n  check: matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (106 terms) at z = 2, 4, 8: max relative difference 1.7e-16\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "ztrans", "ucas": "ztrans n", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ztrans", "in_powers_of_z_1": "z^-1/(1 - 2z^-1 + z^-2)", "region_of_convergence": "|z| > 1", "roc": "|z| > 1", "one_sided": "x[n] for n >= 0", "rules": "n x[n] -> -z X'(z)", "lhs": "Z{n}(z)", "value": "z/(z - 1)^2", "headline": "Z{n}(z) = z/(z - 1)^2"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (106 terms) at z = 2, 4, 8: max relative difference 1.7e-16"}], "files": [], "text": "Z{n}(z) = z/(z - 1)^2\n  in powers of z^-1: z^-1/(1 - 2z^-1 + z^-2)\n  region of convergence: |z| > 1\n  one-sided: x[n] for n >= 0\n  rules: n x[n] -> -z X'(z)\n  check: matches sum_n x[n] z^-n (106 terms) at z = 2, 4, 8: max relative difference 1.7e-16\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "sum(n, 1, inf, 1/n^2)\n  converges absolutely: p-series 1/n^2 with p = 2 > 1\n  partial sums: S_10 = 1.549767731, S_1000 = 1.643934567\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "converge", "ucas": "converge 1/n^2", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "converge", "converges_absolutely": "p-series 1/n^2 with p = 2 > 1", "partial_sums": "S_10 = 1.549767731, S_1000 = 1.643934567", "headline": "sum(n, 1, inf, 1/n^2)"}, "results": [{"kind": "converge"}, {"kind": "converge", "converges_absolutely": "p-series 1/n^2 with p = 2 > 1", "partial_sums": "S_10 = 1.549767731, S_1000 = 1.643934567", "headline": "sum(n, 1, inf, 1/n^2)"}], "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "sum(n, 1, inf, 1/n^2)\n  converges absolutely: p-series 1/n^2 with p = 2 > 1\n  partial sums: S_10 = 1.549767731, S_1000 = 1.643934567\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "power series sum(n, 1, inf, x^n/n) in x\n  center x = 0; coefficients a_n = 1/n of x^(n)\n  radius of convergence R = 1 (ratio test: |a_(n+1)/a_n| -> 1)\n  at x = -1: converges conditionally (alternating series test (|a_n| decreases to 0); not absolutely: |a_n| ~ C/n (p <= 1))\n  at x = 1: diverges (limit comparison with the harmonic series sum 1/n (p = 1): a_n n -> 1)\n  interval of convergence: [-1, 1)\n  sum = -log(1 - x)    for |x| < 1 (-log(1 - u))\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "radius", "ucas": "radius x^n/n", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "radius", "radius": {"value": 1, "exact": "1"}, "center": {"value": 0, "exact": "0"}, "coefficient": "1/n", "test": "ratio test", "interval_of_convergence": "[-1, 1)", "sum": {"value": "-log(1 - x)", "valid_for": "|x| < 1 (-log(1 - u))"}, "headline": "power series sum(n, 1, inf, x^n/n) in x", "details": ["center x = 0; coefficients a_n = 1/n of x^(n)", "radius of convergence R = 1 (ratio test: |a_(n+1)/a_n| -> 1)", "at x = -1: converges conditionally (alternating series test (|a_n| decreases to 0); not absolutely: |a_n| ~ C/n (p <= 1))", "at x = 1: diverges (limit comparison with the harmonic series sum 1/n (p = 1): a_n n -> 1)"]}, "results": [{"kind": "radius"}, {"kind": "radius", "radius": {"value": 1, "exact": "1"}, "center": {"value": 0, "exact": "0"}, "coefficient": "1/n", "test": "ratio test", "interval_of_convergence": "[-1, 1)", "sum": {"value": "-log(1 - x)", "valid_for": "|x| < 1 (-log(1 - u))"}, "headline": "power series sum(n, 1, inf, x^n/n) in x", "details": ["center x = 0; coefficients a_n = 1/n of x^(n)", "radius of convergence R = 1 (ratio test: |a_(n+1)/a_n| -> 1)", "at x = -1: converges conditionally (alternating series test (|a_n| decreases to 0); not absolutely: |a_n| ~ C/n (p <= 1))", "at x = 1: diverges (limit comparison with the harmonic series sum 1/n (p = 1): a_n n -> 1)"]}], "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "power series sum(n, 1, inf, x^n/n) in x\n  center x = 0; coefficients a_n = 1/n of x^(n)\n  radius of convergence R = 1 (ratio test: |a_(n+1)/a_n| -> 1)\n  at x = -1: converges conditionally (alternating series test (|a_n| decreases to 0); not absolutely: |a_n| ~ C/n (p <= 1))\n  at x = 1: diverges (limit comparison with the harmonic series sum 1/n (p = 1): a_n n -> 1)\n  interval of convergence: [-1, 1)\n  sum = -log(1 - x)    for |x| < 1 (-log(1 - u))\n"}, "isError": false}}
